Falsifies `non_volatile_memory_express::verification::record_head_accepts_only_a_head_the_controller_can_have_reached`.

The defect: `SubmissionQueue::record_head` checks only that the reported head lies inside the ring,
not that it lies between the recorded head and the tail. A controller that reports a head past the
tail then frees slots holding commands it has not read, and the next push overwrites one.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(reachable)`.

diff --git a/src/queues.rs b/src/queues.rs
index a08ca91..2afb579 100644
--- a/src/queues.rs
+++ b/src/queues.rs
@@ -82,12 +82,6 @@ impl SubmissionQueue {
         if head >= self.entries {
             return Err(ImpossibleHeadError { head });
         }
-        // How far each value lies ahead of the recorded head, going round the ring.
-        let entries = u32::from(self.entries);
-        let ahead = |slot: u16| (u32::from(slot) + entries - u32::from(self.head)) % entries;
-        if ahead(head) > ahead(self.tail) {
-            return Err(ImpossibleHeadError { head });
-        }
         self.head = head;
         Ok(())
     }
